});
``

Wait — `dart compile kernel` flags: the hooks runner used `--packages=... --output=... --depfile=... hook.dill <hook.dart>`. I'll use --packages + --output. Platform.resolvedExecutable = the dart VM (root test runs under dart). Good.

And this test would have CAUGHT my bug (RED against the current broken hook), then GREEN after the const fix. Perfect TDD sequence:
1. Add the compile test → run → RED (fails: "Not a constant expression").
2. Fix the hook (drop const on the default arm) → run → GREEN.
3. Re-run the widget tests → GREEN.

markTestSkipped — import package:test/test.dart — available. Yes.

Also note: my current hook's android arm `OS.android => const ['m', 'dl']` — const list with no runtime condition — fine. Default arm must drop const.

Double-check for other const pitfalls in my patch: `flags: [ ... if (os == OS.android) ... ]` — I made it non-const already (upstream had it non-const under the ternary). `defines: const { '_GNU_SOURCE': null, 'CONFIG_VERSION': '"2024-01-13"' }` — const map, no runtime refs — fine (upstream had it const).

